    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Boxhagener Platz, redesigned in 2020, is a Gründerzeit‑style civic square that blends historic architecture with modern green space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.berlin.de/sen/bauen/baukultur/berliner-plaetzeprogramm/boxhagener-platz-1568921.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The square sits in the heart of the Friedrichshain Kiez, a neighborhood named after the nearby Volkspark Friedrichshain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrichshain"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Across the Spree, the Oberbaumbrücke links Kreuzberg and Friedrichshain, serving as a historic road and rail bridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrichshain"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After suffering heavy bombing in World War II, Friedrichshain became a cultural hub with East Germany’s largest cinema, Kosmos, and a major sports complex.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
